         <listPerson>
            <person xml:id="HAN03" sex="1">
               <persName>
                  <forename>William</forename>
                  <surname>Hannam</surname>
               </persName>
               <birth when="1000"></birth>
               <death when="1000"></death>
               <occupation>Lawyer</occupation>
               <note type="editorial">
                  <p>William Hannam was a solicitor and general agents for the West India islands, and an actuary to the masonic society, Piazza-chambers, Covent garden. He acted as the attorney in <persName key="TAB01">Benjamin Tabart's</persName> bankruptcy, and often appears with him in the diary. His attendance at the examination of <persName key="PHI01">Sir Richard Phillips</persName> was likely due to it’s connection to Tabart’s bankruptcy proceedings. </p>
               </note>
               <bibl type="website">Ed Pope History (04/04/2021)(</bibl>
